From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] server: queue a system APC for a thread that cannot be signalled

CORE review: security (wineserver APC delivery in a shared, multi-user prefix).

Found at integration by hklmsd (stage E): in a shared prefix the server runs as
the SYSTEM account and signals a standard user's thread through that user's
sg-procagent. Where it cannot (no agent running, as in the gate harness, or the
agent gone), queue_apc() dropped a system APC to a thread that was not yet
waiting. An I/O completion (APC_ASYNC_IO) dropped that way completed the
blocking read as STATUS_ALERTED: ReadFile on a pipe failed with ERROR_ALERTED
(739) in the middle of the data, at random. hklmsd's restricted-token children
lost their output that way, so the write-restricted case was never checked
(it is refused: 5). origin/main has the same fault.

The APC is now queued when the thread is alive but cannot be signalled; the
thread runs it at its next server call (a blocking read is about to wait).
A thread that is gone (no unix pid) still drops it, as before.

Gate hklmsd (a standard user's pipe now checked: every byte, ends with
ERROR_BROKEN_PIPE; the probe reads its children until the pipe breaks);
mutant SG_MUTANT_APC_DROP_UNSIGNALLED.
---
diff --git a/server/thread.c b/server/thread.c
--- a/server/thread.c
+++ b/server/thread.c
@@ -1153,7 +1153,18 @@ static int queue_apc( struct process *process, struct thread *thread, struct thr
         /* send signal for system APCs if needed */
         if (queue == &thread->system_apc && list_empty( queue ) && !is_in_apc_wait( thread ))
         {
-            if (!send_thread_signal( thread, SIGUSR1 )) return 0;
+            /* Stained Glass OS: a thread of another user's process is signalled through that user's
+             * agent; when it cannot be signalled although it is alive (no agent, or it is gone), the
+             * APC is queued all the same and the thread runs it at its next server call (a blocking
+             * read is about to wait). Dropping it completed the I/O as STATUS_ALERTED, so a ReadFile
+             * on a pipe failed with ERROR_ALERTED (hklmsd's restricted-token children, any pipe of a
+             * standard user's processes without the agent). */
+            if (!send_thread_signal( thread, SIGUSR1 )
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_APC_DROP_UNSIGNALLED
+                && (thread->unix_pid == -1 || !sg_system_prefix || thread->process->peer_uid == getuid())
+#endif
+               )
+                return 0;
         }
         /* cancel a possible previous APC with the same owner */
         if (apc->owner) thread_cancel_apc( thread, apc->owner, apc->call.type );
